{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_bgi2vlrij3z5zbykcoac2rkti5lgj6f4pj7g4unr2ifyzkjpzuwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Translation complete and verified.\n\n## What the C library is\n`c_src/` is a single 986-line file: an **stb_ds**-derived dynamic-array + hash-map implementation (hash index with 8-slot buckets, SipHash-2-4 byte hashing, rotate-based string hashing, string arena/strdup key ownership modes) plus the `strkey`/`sh_geti` driver helpers at the bottom. `include/lib.h` declares only `sh_geti`; the rest of the surface is `extern` declarations inside `lib.c`.\n\n## Definition of done (symbol diff)\nBuilt the C `.so` with CMake and diffed `nm -D --defined-only` against the Rust `.so`:\n\n```\nmissing from Rust: (none)     extra in Rust: (none)     C=16  RUST=16\n```\n\nAll 16 exports match by **name and type (`T`)**: `sh_geti`, `strkey`, `stbds_rand_seed`, `stbds_hash_bytes`, `stbds_hash_string`, `stbds_arrgrowf`, `stbds_arrfreef`, `stbds_hmfree_func`, `stbds_hmget_key`, `stbds_hmget_key_ts`, `stbds_hmput_default`, `stbds_hmput_key`, `stbds_hmdel_key`, `stbds_shmode_func`, `stbds_stralloc`, `stbds_strreset`.\n\n## Deliverable\n`translation/Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, `panic = \"abort\"`) + `translation/src/lib.rs` (1348 lines, 16 `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` functions). Uses libc `realloc`/`free`/`printf`/`sprintf` directly so the header-behind-the-pointer layout, allocator ownership, and stdio buffering are ABI/behaviour identical.\n\n## Bugs deliberately preserved\n- **SipHash sign-extension**: `d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` is an `int` that goes negative when byte 3 has its high bit set, so the assignment to `size_t` sign-extends and fills the upper 32 bits with ones. Reproduced via `c_int_to_size_t()` (both in the block loop and the `case 4:` tail).\n- **Seed cancellation** in `stbds_siphash_bytes` (`v0 ^= K ^ seed` undoes the initial `^ seed`) — kept literal.\n- **`printf(\"%s %d\\n\", strmap[z], strmap[z].value)`** passes the struct by value; under SysV AMD64 the two INTEGER eightbytes land in `rsi`/`rdx`, so `%s` eats `key` and `%d` eats `value`. Reproduced exactly (documented in a comment).\n- `switch` fall-through in the hash tail, the missing `temp_key` update in `hmput_key`'s wrap-around probe loop, `shmode_func` leaking the old table, `hmdel_key`'s unsigned `--used_count`, and live `assert()` (no `NDEBUG` in the C build) → `abort()`.\n\n## Verification beyond compiling\nBuilt one C driver set and linked it against **each** `.so`, then also re-ran the **unmodified C-linked binaries** with the Rust `.so` substituted at load time (renamed, `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`). Byte-identical stdout and identical exit codes on all of:\n\n| Coverage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `sh_geti` at n = 0,1,2,3,5,10,20,40,41,100,257 | identical |\n| `hash_string`/`hash_bytes`: 8 alignments × lengths 0–40, high-bit/0xFF/zero data, multiple seeds (475 lines) | identical |\n| binary map: 4000 randomized put/get/del ops, grow+shrink+rehash+tombstone reuse (4190 lines) | identical |\n| string maps in all 4 modes (NONE/DEFAULT/STRDUP/ARENA), 3000 randomized ops each (6256 lines) | identical |\n| `arrgrowf` capacity sequences for elemsize 1,2,3,7,16,64; arena block-growth state; `rand_seed` interleaving | identical |\n| NULL-entry paths, zero-length map fed to `hmput_default`, table-less get/del, invalid `shmode` values | identical |\n| a driver bug that segfaults | **both crash at the same point with the same 15 lines** |\n\n`c_src/` was never modified (mtimes/sizes unchanged); the scratch C build directory has been removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":116407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":598,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_